    "created_at": "2016-04-12T20:31:37Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-04-12T20:31:37Z",
    "body": "Yeah it's a good question what value the `region` member adds.  There's no mention of it in the [original design notes](https://www.w3.org/wiki/Canvas_hit_testing).  I suspect it's for cases where you want to do hit testing without also having fallback elements but perhaps that's not really a legitimate scenario?\n\nYou still need some identifier to pass to `removeHitRegion` and a string ID seems fine to me (nice not to have to necessarily track some return value identifier `setTimeout` style).\n\nBut we could certainly ship the rest of the feature without exposing `region` on the events, and see if there's demand for that piece.  Like you say, as long as a DOM element is provided per region, then you already know what region was hit from the event.\n",
    "author_association": "NONE",
